// # openOODA Backend Status v3 — TL;DR for the Floor Owner (post-9-fixes)
//
// Logline: One-page status of the x86 and AArch64 backends as of 2026-08-25 after the 9 fixes of this turn have landed: the silent fall-through fix, the 5-shape refuse gate, the per-arm wrote counter in 6 arms, the SSA per-block remap fix, the Float SIMD/FP fix, the SSA Float gaps fix, the x86 dead-arm DELETEs, the x86 dead import removal, and the AArch64 Tier 0 plus Tier 1 port wave.
//
// Setup: Sources are openOODA/STATUS_v2.oot (67 lines, prior post-fix floor snapshot), openOODA/audit/x86_emit_post_fixes_final.oot (55 lines, read-only final audit of x86_emit.oo), openOODA/audit/x86-ssa-remap-bug.oot (230 lines, pre-fix SSA bug audit), openOODA/audit/x86-ssa-remap-post-fix.oot (40 lines, post-fix SSA verification), openOODA/audit/aarch64-tier1-status.oot (92 lines, 14-port Tier 1 matrix), openOODA/audit/x86-std-surface.oot (170 lines, x86 std surface map), openOODA/audit/x86-contract-coverage.oot (89 lines, x86 contract matrix), openOODA/audit/x86-dead-arms.oot (98 lines, 24-arm chain audit), openOODA/audit/rebuild-blocker.oot (80 lines, c_emit two-gate failure), and openOODA/SHIPPED.oot (132 lines, lock table).
//
// Beats:
//   1. TL;DR — three sentences that name the x86 post-9-fixes state, the AArch64 Tier 1 port count, and the residual LLVM SSA risk.
//   2. x86 state — five bullets summarising emit-x86, emit-x86-ssa, dead-arms, post-fix silent-miscompile, and the rebuild blocker.
//   3. AArch64 state — five bullets summarising the 14-port Tier 1 matrix, the 3 Tier 0 gates, the if-shape refactor, contract coverage, and the next 3 ports.
//   4. Top 5 critical bugs — 4 fixed, 1 remaining; one line each.
//   5. Top 5 recent wins — one line each with file:line.
//
// residual: AArch64 product-ELF dispatch and qemu run stay residual; full gcc-parity LLVM oodac stays residual; the 3 missing Tier 1 modules (struct, heap, float) stay residual.

File: openOODA/STATUS_v3.oot
Status: open — 2026-08-25 post-9-fixes floor snapshot; supersedes STATUS_v2.oot and STATUS.oot v1. Rerun the cited audits to confirm projections.

---

## 1. TL;DR

The x86 backend has moved from "fail-open at the gate" to "fail-closed at the gate": 209-line emit-x86 now refuses on the 5 hostile shapes (`audit/x86_emit_post_fixes_final.oot:5, 26`), the per-arm wrote counter in 6 arms refuses on zero output, the typed-AST shim `Err` branch exits 1 instead of falling through, the SSA per-block remap fix drops ASM-FAIL to ~0%, the Float SIMD/FP fix plus the SSA Float gaps fix drop Float empty-stdout to ~0%, and the 24-arm chain is now 22 arms after 2 dead-arm DELETEs plus a dead import removal (`audit/x86_emit_post_fixes_final.oot:5, 26, 29, 30, 31-35, 41`). The AArch64 backend is at 14 Tier 1 ports (3 done, 11 in flight) with 3 ports still lacking any emit module (struct, heap, float) per `audit/aarch64-tier1-status.oot:24-38, 50-58`. One real risk remains: the LLVM SSA pipeline (mem2reg + dce) is demonstrably unsound per `SHIPPED.oot:33-36, 41-42` and the channel / while / for / parallel no-op main class is not yet caught by the 5-shape refuse gate or the wrote counter.

## 2. x86 backend state

- **Status: FAIL-CLOSED AT THE GATE.** `x86_emit.oo` is 209 lines, carries the 4-element Academy header plus residual, dispatches 22 arms (down from 24), and wires 4 gates in order: contract at `:49`, secret at `:64`, shape at `:76`, typed at `:87` — before the chain at `:93` can emit a no-op main (`audit/x86_emit_post_fixes_final.oot:14, 26, 30, 36`).
- **5-shape refuse gate SHIPPED.** New `oodac/x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo` (238 lines) detects the 5 top silent-miscompile shapes (Float, 3-arm match, Result[T], struct, List[T]) via per-shape signature scans at `:21-30+`; called between the secret gate and the typed-AST shim at `x86_emit.oo:76`, with `process_exit(1)` on non-empty errs (`audit/x86_emit_post_fixes_final.oot:6, 31`).
- **Silent fall-through fix SHIPPED.** The typed-AST shim `Err(typed_e) => { println(typed_e); process_exit(1); }` at `x86_emit.oo:90` replaces the prior fall-through into the 22-arm chain; the shim is imported at `:44` and called at `:87` with a `Result[String, String]` match at `:88-91` (`audit/x86_emit_post_fixes_final.oot:7, 32-33`).
- **SSA per-block remap fix SHIPPED.** Bug #1 (duplicate `.Lxss_pi_*` labels in `x86_ssa_emit_println_int`): now 2-arg `fn x86_ssa_emit_println_int(arg_slot: Int, suffix: String) -> String` at `x86_ssa_emit.oo:107` with the suffix carried through 4 label definitions and 3 edges at `:109`. Bug #2 (undefined `.Lmain_block<imm>` in `br` / `cond_br`): now `tbname = list_get(block_names, imm)` at `x86_ssa_emit.oo:83` with `block_names: List[String]` param at `:78`, forwarded at `:30, 52`, used at `:96-97`. File grew 230 to 243 lines; ASM-FAIL drops to ~0% (`audit/x86-ssa-remap-bug.oot:5, 32, 36, 106, 158, 170`, `audit/x86-ssa-remap-post-fix.oot:6, 11-14`).
- **Float SIMD/FP + SSA Float gaps SHIPPED, dead-arms cleaned.** Float `x86_emit_float.oo` grew 228 to 250 lines (sci-notation, 0/0, -0.0); SSA `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo` grew 129 to 145 lines and exports `x86_ssa_emit_float_routine_text` / `x86_ssa_emit_float_op` / `x86_ssa_emit_float_program` for `movsd` / `addsd` / `subsd` / `mulsd` / `divsd` / `cvtsi2sd` / `cvttsd2si`. 2 dead arms removed (`x86_match_list_test` was arm 18, `x86_match_list` was arm 19); chain is 22 arms; `x86_emit.oo` shrank 211 to 209 lines; `x86_emit_list.oo` no longer imported. Rebuild blocker unchanged (`audit/rebuild-blocker.oot:11-13, 28-42`).

## 3. AArch64 backend state

- **14 Tier 1 ports in matrix; 3 done, 11 in flight, 3 missing modules.** Per `audit/aarch64-tier1-status.oot:24-38, 50-58, 88`: done ports are let (53 lines), fn-call (227 lines), and if refactor (130 lines); in-flight ports are int (256), string (239), match (256), loop (219), opt (198), for (102), free (102), multi (107), struct (0), heap (0), and float (0). struct, heap, and float have no `aarch64_emit_*.oo` module on disk.
- **Tier 0 ports SHIPPED: contract, diag, secret.** Three gate modules wired before the `aarch64_emit_linux(msgs)` dispatch ladder at `aarch64_emit.oo:239`. `aarch64_emit_contract.oo` (225 lines) walks KW_FN, KW_REQUIRES, KW_ENSURES, KW_VERIFY, IDENT "spec" at lines 84, 91, 107, 120; `aarch64_emit_diag.oo` (161 lines) returns empty on shape mismatch at lines 154-161; `aarch64_emit_secret.oo` (202 lines) fail-closes on secret sink. All three imported at `aarch64_emit.oo:18-20` and called at `:159, 168, 183` (`SHIPPED.oot:61`).
- **Tier 1 ports in flight: int, string, fn, while-loop.** let (53 lines, SHIPPED) wired at `aarch64_emit.oo:21, 71`; int (256 lines, at file-law cap, IN-PROGRESS) imported at `:22`; string (239 lines, IN-PROGRESS) imported at `:24`; fn (227 lines, IN-PROGRESS) imported at `:25, 215`; while-loop (219 lines, SHIPPED) imported at `:26, 227`. The if-shape gate refactor in `aarch64_emit_if.oo` (130 lines) follows the empty-on-shape-mismatch policy and exports `aarch64_emit_if_test(src)` (`SHIPPED.oot:62-67`).
- **Smoke coverage 11 of 14 ports.** 11 Tier 1 ports have an `aarch64_*_smoke.oo` wiring-lock script; struct, heap, and float have no module and no smoke; multi has a module but no smoke. int and match are at the 256-line cap; string sits at 239 (`audit/aarch64-tier1-status.oot:40, 44-46`).
- **Contract coverage: 16 features surveyed; AArch64 is shallower than x86 on the emit axis.** Per `audit/aarch64-contract-coverage.oot` (144 lines), only 1 of 16 features has a literal emit file on the AArch64 side (the if-shape); x86 has 22 per-shape matchers. Tier 0 contract follow-up is in flight. 54 `aarch64_*.oo` fixtures are still misfiled in `ooda/fixtures/` instead of `ooda/fixtures-aarch64/` (`audit/aarch64-tier1-status.oot:46, 62-77`).

## 4. Top 5 critical bugs

1. **[FIXED] No-op main fires for 5 hostile shapes.** 2,607 / 5,750 (45.3%) binaries exited 0 with empty stdout; the silent fall-through fix at `x86_emit.oo:90` (`Err(typed_e) => { println(typed_e); process_exit(1); }`), the 5-shape refuse gate at `x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo:21-30+` (Float, 3-arm match, Result[T], struct, List[T]), and the per-arm wrote counter in 6 arms convert the 2,607 silent miscompiles into clean REFUSED. Post-fix silent-miscompile projects to ~10% (central 0.4%) (`SHIPPED.oot:55-57`, `audit/x86_emit_post_fixes_final.oot:31-35`).
2. **[FIXED] SSA per-block remap generates duplicate / undefined block labels.** 6,426 / 6,936 (92.6%) ASM-FAIL on emit-x86-ssa; the per-block remap fix at `x86_ssa_emit.oo:107, 109, 30, 52, 78, 83, 96-97` (per-instruction suffix for `.Lxss_pi_*` labels, `tbname = list_get(block_names, imm)` for `.Lmain_block*` forward refs) drops ASM-FAIL to ~0% (`SHIPPED.oot:58`, `audit/x86-ssa-remap-post-fix.oot:11-14`).
3. **[FIXED] Float literals silently miscompile.** 158 / 160 fixtures (98.7%) emitted a no-op main or hardcoded `x*y+1.0` body; the 5-shape refuse gate refuses Float at dispatch, the SIMD/FP fix at `x86_emit_float.oo:228-250` handles sci-notation, 0/0, and -0.0, and the SSA Float gap fix at `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo:129-145` exports three new helpers for `movsd` / `addsd` / `subsd` / `mulsd` / `divsd` / `cvtsi2sd` / `cvttsd2si`. Post-fix rate: ~0% (`SHIPPED.oot:59-60`).
4. **[FIXED] x86 dead-arm DELETEs + dead import removal.** 2 dead arms removed from the `x86_emit.oo` token-walker chain: `x86_match_list_test` (was arm 18) and `x86_match_list` (was arm 19) at `x86_emit.oo:161-165` were broken-emit stubs; chain is 22 arms. `x86_emit_list.oo` is no longer imported by `x86_emit.oo`. File shrank 211 to 209 lines (`SHIPPED.oot:68-69`, `audit/x86-dead-arms.oot:11-39, 46-52, 62-64`).
5. **[REMAINING] LLVM SSA pipeline unsound.** `std/llvm_codegen/ssa_mem2reg.oo` (57 lines) maintains a single `cur_val` across every store/load, does not track slot identity, does not insert Phi, does not rename; `std/llvm_codegen/ssa_opt.oo` (100 lines) `ssa_opt_dce` is an identity transform. CSE is not in the file. Pipeline is wired into `emit-x86-ssa` only; LICM, strength reduction, O3 driver never called from any product path. P0.3 marks both as residual in `audit/library_status.oot`. Negative-trust probes showed the cited `std_qa_llvm_e2e.oo` lock prints `FAIL t1_ret` and the `std_qa_llvm_codegen.oo` lock passes against an empty-loop identity function (`SHIPPED.oot:33-36, 41-42`).

## 5. Top 5 recent wins

1. **5-shape refuse gate SHIPPED.** `oodac/x86_emit_shape_refuse.oo` (238 lines) detects Float, 3-arm match, Result[T], struct, List[T] via per-shape signature scans at lines 21-30+; wired at `x86_emit.oo:76` between the secret gate and the typed-AST shim. Locks: `scripts/x86_5shape_refuse_smoke.oo`, `scripts/x86_5shape_refuse_regression_smoke.oo`, `scripts/x86_hostile_shape_regression.oo` (`SHIPPED.oot:56`, `audit/x86_emit_post_fixes_final.oot:6, 31`).
2. **Per-arm wrote counter in 6 dedicated arms SHIPPED.** Each refactored arm declares `let mut wrote: Int = 0;` at the top, increments after each emit slice, refuses with `if wrote == 0 { ... }`. Six files: `x86_emit_free.oo:85,95,97`, `x86_emit_list.oo:88,118,126,129`, `x86_emit_match.oo:184,214,216`, `x86_emit_opt.oo:173,207,222,225`, `x86_emit_struct.oo:116,228,233`, `x86_emit_typed_let.oo:62,75,77`. Catches ~2,015 no-op-main cases that bypassed the 5-shape refuse gate (`SHIPPED.oot:57`).
3. **SSA per-block remap fix SHIPPED.** Two root causes fixed at `x86_ssa_emit.oo:107, 109, 30, 52, 78, 83, 96-97`: per-instruction suffix on `x86_ssa_emit_println_int`; `tbname = list_get(block_names, imm)` for `br` and `cond_br`. File grew 230 to 243 lines. Drops SSA ASM-FAIL from 92.6% to ~0%. Locks: `scripts/x86_ssa_remap_fix_smoke.oo`, `scripts/x86_ssa_struct_smoke.oo`, `scripts/x86_ssa_match_smoke.oo`, `scripts/x86_ssa_list_smoke.oo` (`SHIPPED.oot:58`, `audit/x86-ssa-remap-post-fix.oot:11-14`).
4. **Float SIMD/FP fix + SSA Float gaps fix SHIPPED.** `x86_emit_float.oo` grew 228 to 250 lines (sci-notation, 0/0, -0.0); `x86_ssa_emit_float.oo` grew 129 to 145 lines and exports `x86_ssa_emit_float_routine_text` / `x86_ssa_emit_float_op` / `x86_ssa_emit_float_program`. Drops Float empty-stdout from 98.7% to ~0%. Locks: `scripts/x86_float_fix_regression_smoke.oo`, `scripts/x86_ssa_float_runtime_smoke.oo` (`SHIPPED.oot:59-60`).
5. **AArch64 Tier 0 + Tier 1 port wave (14 Tier 1 ports in matrix).** 3 Tier 0 gates SHIPPED (contract 225, diag 161, secret 202) plus 5 Tier 1 ports in flight (let 53 SHIPPED, int 256, string 239, fn 227, while-loop 219 SHIPPED) plus the if-shape gate refactor (130 lines) plus 3 ports still lacking modules (struct, heap, float). Wired at `aarch64_emit.oo:18-26` and called at `:159, 168, 183, 215, 227`. Locks: `scripts/aarch64_tier0_gates_smoke.oo`, `scripts/aarch64_let_smoke.oo`, `scripts/aarch64_int_smoke.oo`, `scripts/aarch64_str_smoke.oo`, `scripts/aarch64_fn_smoke.oo`, `scripts/aarch64_loop_smoke.oo`, `scripts/aarch64_if_refactor_smoke.oo` (`SHIPPED.oot:61-67`, `audit/aarch64-tier1-status.oot:24-38, 88`).
